 171 | ## Section 3 — Open / Pending (Not Yet Started)
 172 | 
 173 | ### 🔴 TODO-P1 — Provider Health Monitoring + Auto-Failover Alerting
 174 | **Context:** `core/router.py` has tiered failover logic but no persistent health state. If Gemini quota is exhausted and router silently falls to Tier 3 (OpenRouter), the user has no visibility until a response is slow or wrong.
 175 | **Risk:** Silent quality degradation — user sends a complex task, gets Tier 3 response without knowing.
 176 | **Priority:** 🔴 P1 — runtime reliability
 177 | 
 178 | **Jules spec:**
 179 | ```
 180 | Files to change: core/router.py, tools/monitor.py (or create tools/provider_health.py)
 181 | Goal: Track per-provider success/failure rates with a rolling 10-minute window.
 182 |   - Add a ProviderHealthTracker class (or extend existing Router):
 183 |       * Records last N=20 calls per provider: success/failure + latency
 184 |       * Exposes health_summary() dict: {provider: {ok_rate, avg_latency, last_error}}
 185 |   - When a provider fails 3 consecutive times, emit a Telegram alert:
 186 |       "⚠️ Provider {name} degraded. Routing to fallback tier."
 187 |   - When provider recovers (1 success after failure streak), log recovery.
 188 |   - Persist health state to data/provider_health.json (overwrite on each update)
 189 |   - Do NOT change existing routing logic — tracker is observability only
 190 |   - Do NOT touch .env, interfaces/, guardian_engine.py, or crons/
 191 |   - Acceptance: curl NinaGate with a bad provider key, confirm Telegram alert fires within 60s
 192 | ```
