 196 | ### 🔴 TODO-P1 — Governance Index Auto-Update (54 files missing tests)
 197 | **Context:** Pre-push hook reports 54 files requiring tests with no matching test file found. This is a governance integrity issue — the index claims coverage that doesn't exist.
 198 | **Risk:** Test coverage claims in docs are false. Governance score (81.1%) is inflated.
 199 | **Approach:** Don't write 54 test files — that's noise. Write a governance reconciler that marks files as `"test_required": false` in the index if they are infra/tooling scripts (not logic-bearing), so the warning count reflects real gaps only.
 200 | **Priority:** 🔴 P1 — governance integrity
 201 | 
 202 | **Jules spec:**
 203 | ```
 204 | File to change: tools/validate_index.py (and governance_index.json if it exists)
 205 | Goal: Add a "test_exempt" classification for files that are tooling/infra scripts:
 206 |   - Read the index; for each file flagged as "requires_tests" with no test file:
 207 |       * If file is in crons/ or tools/ AND its only public functions are CLI entrypoints
 208 |         (i.e., if __name__ == "__main__" pattern), mark as test_exempt: true
 209 |       * If file is in interfaces/ and is a pure adapter (no business logic), mark exempt
 210 |   - Re-run validate_index: only files with real logic gaps should warn
 211 |   - Do NOT delete any test requirements — only reclassify based on code pattern analysis
 212 |   - Output: updated governance_index.json + console summary "X real gaps, Y exempted"
 213 |   - Do NOT touch .env, guardian_engine.py, main.py, or core/router.py
 214 | ```
