 227 | ### 🟠 TODO-P2 — NinaGate System Template — Wire to Jules Dispatch
 228 | **Context:** `ninagate/system_templates.json` defines NINA's identity contract. But when `tools/jules.py` dispatches a new task, the `prompt` payload does NOT inject this system template. Jules receives raw task text with no NINA identity framing.
 229 | **Effect:** Jules-generated code/PRs don't know NINA's conventions (append-only logs, no heredoc, conventional commits, etc.) unless the task prompt manually includes them — which is fragile.
 230 | **Priority:** 🟠 P2
 231 | 
 232 | **Jules spec:**
 233 | ```
 234 | File: tools/jules.py — function: run_dispatch
 235 | Goal: Before sending the dispatch prompt to Jules API, prepend the NINA system template:
 236 |   - Read ninagate/system_templates.json at dispatch time (not at import time)
 237 |   - Extract the "system" role content
 238 |   - Prepend it to the prompt as: f"[NINA CONTEXT]\n{system_content}\n\n[TASK]\n{prompt}"
 239 |   - Keep prompt length within 8000 chars total — truncate system template if needed
 240 |     (truncate from the bottom of the template, not the task)
 241 |   - Do NOT change anything in ninagate/main.py or core/router.py
 242 |   - Do NOT touch .env, guardian_engine.py, or interfaces/
 243 |   - Acceptance: dispatch a test task; confirm PR description or Jules output references
 244 |     NINA conventions (append-only logs, conventional commits)
 245 | ```
 246 | 
